<start_of_turn>model
","When \( \text{H}_2\text{S} \) gas is passed into a mixture of \( \text{Mn}^{2+}, \text{\text{Ni}}^{2+}, \text{Cu}^{2+}, \) and \( \text{Hg}^{2+} \) ions in an acidic aqueous solution, the following products will precipitate:  
1. **\( \text{Mn}^{2+} \):**  
   - \( \text{Mg}^{2+} \) ions react with \( \text{H}_2\text{S} \) to form \( \text{MnO}_2 \) (manganese dioxide) which is a precipitate.  
   - \( \text{Mn}^{2+} + 2\text{H}_2\text{S} \rightarrow \text{MnO}_2 + 2\text{H}_2\text{O} \)  

2. **\( \text{Cu}^{2+} \):**  
   - \( \text{Cu}^{2+} \) ions react with \( \text{H}_2\text{S} \) to form \( \text{CrS} \) (chromium sulfide) which is a precipitate.  
   - \( \text{Cu}^{2+} + 2\text{H}_2\text{S} \rightarrow \text{CrS} + 2\text{H}_2\text{O} \)  

3. **\( \text{Hg}^{2+} \):**  
   - \( \text{Hg}^{2+} \) ions react with \( \text{H}_2\text{S} \) to form \( \text{HgS} \) (hydrogen sulfide) which is a precipitate.  
   - \( \text{Hg}^{2+} + 2\text{H}_2\text{S} \rightarrow \text{HgS} + 2\text{H}_2\text{O} \)  

4. **\( \text{Ni}^{2+} \):**  
   - \( \text{Ni}^{2+} \) ions do not precipitate from \( \text{H}_2\text{S} \) in acidic solutions.  
   - \( \text{Ni}^{2+} + 2\text{H}_2\text{S} \rightarrow \text{NiS} + 2\text{H}_2\text{O} \) (but this does not precipitate in acidic solutions)  

Thus, the precipitates are:  
- \( \text{MnO}_2 \) (from \( \text{Mn}^{2+} \))  
- \( \text{CrS} \) (from \( \text{Cu}^{2+} \))  
- \( \text{HgS} \) (from \( \text{Hg}^{2+} \))  

The correct answer is:  
\(\boxed{\text{MnO}_2, \text{CrS}, \text{HgS}}\)",fluency,"# Task Description
