\[
\nabla \times \mathbf{V} = \frac{\partial \mathbf{V}_z}{\partial x} - \frac{\partial \mathbf{V}_y}{\partial y}
\]
where \(\mathbf{V} = \mathbf{V}_x + \mathbf{V}_y + \mathbf{V}_z\). 

Since \(\mathbf{V}\) depends only on \(x\) and \(y\), the \(z\)-component is zero, i.e., \(\mathbf{V}_z = 0\). Thus, the curl simplifies to:
\[
\nabla \times \mathbf{V} = \frac{\partial 0}{\partial x} - \frac{\partial \mathbf{V}_y}{\partial y} = 0 - \frac{\partial \mathbf{V}_y}{\partial y} = -\frac{\partial \mathbf{V}_y}{\partial y}.
\]
